<%# The problem in podcasters' words. Paraphrased from public r/podcasting threads and labelled so (R70): never
    presented as verbatim testimonials, never attributed to a person. %>
<section id="quotes" class="quotes" aria-labelledby="quotes-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 id="quotes-title" class="quotes-title">
      What podcasters say <span class="quotes-source">— paraphrased from r/podcasting, 2026</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="quotes-grid">
      <blockquote class="quote">
        <p>Brands keep dropping hints that we're not really big enough.</p>
      </blockquote>
      <blockquote class="quote">
        <p>We spend months reaching out and sending media kits, then maybe land one sponsor for one episode.</p>
      </blockquote>
      <blockquote class="quote">
        <p>Sponsorship pricing feels like a mysterious formula.</p>
      </blockquote>
    </div>
    <p class="quotes-coda">
      Only 39% of podcasters make money from their show, and 48% of the rest say their audience is too small.
      <span class="quotes-cite">RSS.com podcaster survey</span>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
